.TH OPM 1 "August 2026" "Open Partition Manager 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
opm \- open-source partition management tool
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B opm
\fIcommand\fR [options]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Open Partition Manager
is an open-source tool for creating, deleting, resizing, moving, formatting,
checking, cloning, and recovering partitions on Linux, macOS, and Windows.
It reads and writes MBR and GPT partition tables and supports the FAT32,
NTFS, ext4, exFAT, and Linux swap filesystems.
.SH DEVICE COMMANDS
.TP
.B list
List all disks and partitions.
.TP
.B info \fIdevice\fR
Show device information.
.TP
.B read \fIdevice\fR
Read and display the partition table.
.TP
.B mklabel \fIdevice\fR \fImbr|gpt\fR
Write a new (empty) partition table.
.SH PARTITION COMMANDS
.TP
.B create \fIdevice\fR \fIstart\fR \fIsize\fR \fItype\fR [name]
Create a partition (type: ntfs, fat32, linux, swap, efi, lvm, raid).
.TP
.B delete \fIdevice\fR \fInumber\fR
Delete a partition.
.TP
.B resize \fIdevice\fR \fInumber\fR \fIsize\fR
Resize a partition.
.TP
.B move \fIdevice\fR \fInumber\fR \fIstart\fR
Move a partition, preserving its data.
.TP
.B convert \fIdevice\fR \fImbr|gpt\fR
Convert the partition table in place (data preserved).
.TP
.B set-active \fIdevice\fR \fInumber\fR [on|off]
Toggle the MBR bootable flag.
.TP
.B hide / unhide \fIdevice\fR \fInumber\fR
Hide or unhide a FAT-family partition.
.SH FILESYSTEM COMMANDS
.TP
.B format \fIdevice\fR \fIfs\fR \fIstart\fR [size] [label]
Format a partition (fs: fat32, ntfs, ext4, exfat, swap).
.TP
.B check \fIdevice\fR \fIstart\fR
Check a filesystem.
.TP
.B fsinfo \fIdevice\fR \fIstart\fR
Show filesystem information.
.TP
.B label \fIdevice\fR \fIstart\fR \fIname\fR
Set the volume label.
.TP
.B undelete \fIdevice\fR \fIstart\fR [\-\-restore \fIindex\fR]
List and recover deleted FAT files.
.TP
.B cryptinfo \fIdevice\fR \fIstart\fR
Detect encryption (BitLocker/LUKS).
.TP
.B align \fIdevice\fR [\-\-fix]
Report 4K alignment; \fB\-\-fix\fR moves unaligned partitions.
.SH SYSTEM COMMANDS
.TP
.B recover \fIdevice\fR [\-\-rebuild]
Scan for lost partitions; rebuild an MBR table with \fB\-\-rebuild\fR.
.TP
.B luks open|close|status
Manage LUKS volumes via cryptsetup.
.TP
.B bitlocker unlock \fIdevice\fR [mount]
Unlock a BitLocker volume via dislocker.
.TP
.B boot-repair \-\-uefi [\-\-add ...]
List or create UEFI boot entries via efibootmgr.
.TP
.B reset-password \-\-linux \fIshadow\fR \fIuser\fR [pass]
Reset a Linux password (SHA-512 hash, atomic write).
.TP
.B reset-password \-\-windows \fIsam\fR [user]
Reset a Windows password via chntpw.
.TP
.B lvm, raid
List LVM physical volumes / software RAID arrays.
.TP
.B i18n [locale] [catalog]
Manage message catalogs.
.SH SIZES
Sizes accept byte suffixes: \fB512M\fR, \fB10G\fR, \fB2T\fR, or plain bytes.
.SH GUI
Run \fBopm-gui\fR for the graphical interface with wizards, a visual
partition map, operation log, and light/dark themes.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, non-zero on error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gdisk (8),
.BR fdisk (8),
.BR mkfs (8)
.SH AUTHOR
Open Partition Manager contributors (https://github.com/omiinaya/open-disk-manager)
